{"name":"Muntok White Pepper","hex":"#d2a172","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"pepper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the family Piperaceae.","A spice prepared from the fermented, dried, unripe berries of this plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add pepper to.","To strike with something made up of small particles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pepper"}],"entries":[{"title":"White Pepper","blocks":[{"text":"White Pepper is the seventh studio album by the American rock band Ween, and the last album they released on Elektra Records. It was released on May 2, 2000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1e/Ween-WhitePepper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Pepper","wikidata":"Q7995190"},{"title":"Black pepper","blocks":[{"text":"Black pepper is a flowering vine in the family Piperaceae, cultivated for its fruit, which is usually dried and used as a spice and seasoning. The fruit is a drupe (stonefruit) which is about 5 mm in diameter, dark red, and contains a stone which encloses a single pepper seed. Peppercorns and the ground pepper derived from them may be described simply as pepper, or more precisely as black pepper, green pepper, or white pepper."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Piper_nigrum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-107.jpg/330px-Piper_nigrum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-107.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_pepper","wikidata":"Q43084"},{"title":"Muntok","blocks":[{"text":"Muntok or, more commonly, Mentok is a town in the Indonesian province of Bangka-Belitung on the island of Sumatra. The capital of West Bangka Regency, it is the site of the biggest tin smelter on the world. Mentok refers to the tip of the island."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/%E5%8D%B0%E5%B0%BC%E9%82%A6%E5%8A%A0%E5%B3%B6%E6%96%87%E5%B3%B6%E5%BB%A3%E7%A6%8F%E5%BB%9F%E8%88%87%E8%B3%88%E7%91%AA%E6%B8%85%E7%9C%9F%E5%AF%BA.jpg/330px-%E5%8D%B0%E5%B0%BC%E9%82%A6%E5%8A%A0%E5%B3%B6%E6%96%87%E5%B3%B6%E5%BB%A3%E7%A6%8F%E5%BB%9F%E8%88%87%E8%B3%88%E7%91%AA%E6%B8%85%E7%9C%9F%E5%AF%BA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muntok","wikidata":"Q1948643"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg/1280px-Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black pepper vine climbing on jackfruit tree (Artocarpus heterophyllus)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg/1280px-Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Single stem with flowers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/4_color_mix_of_peppercorns.jpg/500px-4_color_mix_of_peppercorns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/4_color_mix_of_peppercorns.jpg/1280px-4_color_mix_of_peppercorns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/4_color_mix_of_peppercorns.jpg/500px-4_color_mix_of_peppercorns.